<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n47320" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tābĕfăcĭo</span></b> ,
			fēci, 3, v. a.
		tabes-facio, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to melt</i>, <i>dissolve.</i>—<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tabefac audaciam virtutis eorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg. 1
					Macc. 4, 32</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vigilia honestatis tabefaciet carnes,</span>”
				<i>subdue</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id. Ecclus. 31, 1</span></i>
			.—Hence, Part.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tābē^factus</span></b> , a,
			um, <i>melted</i>, <i>dissolved</i> (post-class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tabefactis nivibus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sol. 2 <i>med.</i></span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cadaver in suo sanguine,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Jud. 14, 14</span></i>
			.</div>
